11. Sign In Flow

The sign-in interface is frontend-only.

The detailed sign-in/profile form collects:

Full name

Job title

Email address

Phone number

Company

Department

Password

Confirm password

Remember me

Terms acceptance

Validation includes:

required fields

minimum password length

password confirmation match

terms acceptance

On successful submission, the entered profile data is passed into the current frontend user state.

No real credentials are stored or authenticated.

12. User Profile Flow

My Profile is a separate modal component.

It displays/edit fields based on the currently logged-in frontend user:

Full name

Job title

Email

Phone

Company

Department

Saving profile changes updates the current frontend user state so the Topbar identity and Profile modal stay synchronized during the active session.

13. Settings Flow

Settings is a separate modal component.

Demo preferences include:

Email notifications

Activity updates

Compact mode

These are frontend-only UI preferences in V1.

14. Logout Flow

Log Out opens a separate confirmation modal.

After confirmation:

loggedIn = false

The avatar/profile menu disappears and the Sign In control becomes visible.

No real authentication session is terminated because V1 has no backend authentication.

